if jenkins agent with amazon or any other linux flavours
create a disk
attach the disk to the instance
install lvm2

create a pv (persistant voolume)
```
pvcreate /dev/<name of the disk>
```
here our disk name is pvcreate /dev/nvme1n1p1

create a vg (volume group)
```
vgcreate <name of the volume group> <name of the persistant volume>
```
here our vg name is -> "jenkins_vg" and pv is -> "/dev/nvme1n1p1"

we can also create a specific size of logical volume by mentioning the size while creatig the volume.
```
sudo lvcreate -L <Size> -n <LV_Name> <VG_Name>
example :
sudo lvcreate -L 20G -n jenkins_lv jenkins_vg
```

create a logical volume from that volume group with full space like 100% free disk of size full or any size like 2G or 10G etc
```
lvcreate -l 100%FREE -n <name of logical volume> <name of volume group>
```
here our logical volume gets created from this lvcreate -l 100%FREE -n jenkins_lv jenkins_vg (with full disk space)

make filesystem for that logical volume based on the filesystem type ex: xfs or ext4
for newer versions of linux this will be "ext4"
```
mkfs.xfs <location to the logical volume>
or
mkfs.ext4 <location to the logical volume>
```
here our location ot the logical volume is "/dev/jenkins_vg/jenkins_lv"

then mount the volume to a desired directory or folder
```
mount <location of the logical volume> <location of the desired directory or folder>
```
here our logical vol location is "/dev/jenkins_vg/jenkins_lv" and being mounted to "/home/ec2-user/jenkins"
```
mount /dev/jenkins_vg/jenkins_lv /home/ec2-user/jenkins
```

get the block id of the logical volume
```
blkid <location of the logical volume>
```
here ours is: blkid /dev/jenkins_vg/jenkins_lv

add that UUID and other file system details to "/etc/fstab"
```
example -> UUID=23661009-59dc-4c1b-a0aa-04ff2e92b40e /home/ec2-user/jenkins ext4 defaults,nofail 0 2
```

finally mount the volume with this command at the end
```
sudo mount -a
```